{"skill":{"slug":"openclaw-memory","displayName":"Openclaw Memory"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770894316486,"changelog":"- Initial release of openclaw-memory: persistent memory system for OpenClaw agents with semantic search and x402 payment integration.\n- Supports both Free (100 memories, 7-day retention) and Pro (unlimited, permanent) tiers.\n- Features local storage with SQLite and vector embeddings for semantic retrieval.\n- Provides command-line tools and a web dashboard for managing memories.\n- All data is stored locally with full privacy and no external telemetry.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"AGENT-PAYMENTS.md","size":13404,"sha256":"ff8f068c02badf97e44bbc87b79d1f7555a3ae8b84a7b3fab2185db9cf7b35d6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hooks/request-after.js","size":2737,"sha256":"4ea55d79257670881a8fc7f3ef677b42cbd102f974a5be98872b34a44f54286b","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"hooks/request-before.js","size":1983,"sha256":"8c11d0afa0a8fdfce2f6959e0841fa5181fe8e80a614e7c3bbb9226b59f5985b","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"hooks/session-end.js","size":2642,"sha256":"1012a3d9f316ad01511574bea2d0dfe0e512f7fd0372ce44c46208a54681f71e","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"IMPLEMENTATION-SUMMARY.md","size":7305,"sha256":"43a58e25f1ac6a764891ef73b492ea5b5510f89f542ce99a6b89209c3a9ca80b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md","size":5144,"sha256":"681ddf6103aa1d8aabedf6b1e7b47e8455814598b05c8ee8120d7e080500175a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"migrations/001-init.sql","size":3284,"sha256":"900e434eec1c4adc768490fbde9dc65bd357b2637b776f83088ca4818ff385ef","contentType":"application/sql"},{"path":"migrations/002-x402-payments.sql","size":1579,"sha256":"7e16e10821e9a84718eda7b1a06b4e745c57bc6fdbada37b6bd3627baebac0e8","contentType":"application/sql"},{"path":"package.json","size":1096,"sha256":"f296abe4b65730b9d006c31555c0bcfe8a49b2e3bc141fcdef1f40e32400fd19","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"README.md","size":11740,"sha256":"c3f674634fe0bbbe1812b033bb079e8f494f95ac550539b3e8c5ea2f047199db","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3394,"sha256":"f2bd1d9111754434a63df292e0c21b22375946b6847e96415d7b62f137bb83e3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"src/analyzer.js","size":15327,"sha256":"6d90cd1f6e9e1e10b2ddfb15c150d9f03068126afedac242a3729a8d80e67a57","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/cli.js","size":12112,"sha256":"ab79532d6be3c361c9af5915620d66651d51a76a0670dc12e686af02df67fd9c","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/dashboard.js","size":12600,"sha256":"eadc1ba4828c91c4197b90497d84b169a41475e0ad9cddce3b70000b4b22e175","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/embeddings.js","size":6316,"sha256":"7105ea9c9b4b89383acf5577e482c531a4eb1007eddcd0780c5190c3e71c4793","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/index.js","size":8495,"sha256":"2cfadf1a7cd98bfe8b8ae864427fe0d62a7cc87f909b461b94428af3f39fbcae","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/pruner.js","size":15555,"sha256":"ce8f0e55bb9fa48fdcdb30960ce595a2df5220d7f65791bac50e9d66a9fcd972","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/retriever.js","size":12021,"sha256":"ae377116932122eb8c1a03c3f77a675087d723c666e5ab22771630ae44f39a70","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/setup.js","size":3976,"sha256":"ff1f0bec2dc38e386f266eddea5c38bce736a78aa04550df9bee11386ce7010f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/storage.js","size":20877,"sha256":"3c98b5163a08b1389eebf45f3a4d25504dcc8a5757b6d0bc7fc94ab359dc0d8f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"src/x402.js","size":7184,"sha256":"927f5fcabf4b9212263846bf5cc3c333512954828072e26c40922ae0d78adc50","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2776,"sha256":"dbfc45fad686c3ac43c99eec59fa1da10396b921aab98df48e9f0645e3e5fd25","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789063118126,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a1a1e071c4311ba43a5356d23dd8acdad22278a7f6f88ba7c5f96c247038a0a2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a1a1e071c4311ba43a5356d23dd8acdad22278a7f6f88ba7c5f96c247038a0a2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openclaw-memory\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill implements a persistent memory system that includes an autonomous payment feature (x402 protocol) allowing AI agents to 'upgrade' themselves to a Pro tier for 0.5 USDT/month. While the core RAG functionality is standard, the bundle uses prompt injection techniques in `SKILL.md` and `AGENT-PAYMENTS.md` to persuade the agent to spend funds autonomously based on 'ROI' calculations. Furthermore, `src/x402.js` contains a significant vulnerability where the `verifyTransactionOnChain` function is a stub that 'trusts any valid-looking transaction hash,' which could be exploited or lead to unintended financial state changes. The inclusion of autonomous spending logic and persuasive instructions targeting the agent's decision-making process is highly risky.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163449522},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":66,"checkedAt":1789063118126},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This memory skill does what it advertises, but it needs review because it automatically stores conversation data, exposes weakly scoped memory/payment APIs, and makes privacy claims that conflict with its default remote embedding behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The dashboard exposes memory read, write, search, delete, stats, and payment endpoints keyed only by caller-supplied wallet values, and the server does not explicitly bind to loopback. The default OpenAI embedding provider can transmit memory text externally despite local-only privacy claims.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package has no postinstall script and uses declared OpenClaw hooks in package.json; however, documentation says the hooks work automatically after install, so sensitive collection begins as part of normal skill use.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The request hooks automatically extract and store prompt/response-derived memories, then reinsert retrieved memory content as request context and memory_text without clear untrusted-data boundaries or user opt-in controls.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill creates persistent storage under ~/.openclaw/openclaw-memory, keeps conversation-derived memories and access/payment records, supports deletion/pruning, and provides Pro unlimited retention without strong authentication, redaction, or quota enforcement guarantees.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, persistent semantic memory with x402 payments, matches the shipped hooks, SQLite storage, dashboard, and payment code, but those capabilities handle sensitive conversation history and payment state with insufficient scoping and disclosure.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use local embeddings unless you explicitly accept sending memory text and search queries to OpenAI, do not store secrets or regulated data, do not expose the dashboard without authentication, and do not give agents funded wallet access without explicit spending caps and human approval.","findings":"[MP3] expected: Memory creation, retrieval, deletion, and pruning are expected for a memory skill, but the concern is partly supported because stored memory content can later be injected into agent context without a clear trust boundary.\n[SQP-2] expected: Automatic learning and agent payments are disclosed features, but the artifacts under-disclose consent, redaction, wallet-spending limits, and human-approval expectations for sensitive data and irreversible payments.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The privacy documentation says data stays local and nothing is sent to external servers, while the code defaults to OpenAI embeddings and sends text to the OpenAI embeddings API when configured with an API key.\n[T02] unexpected: Persistent memory is expected, but unauthenticated writes for arbitrary agent_wallet values and later verbatim reinjection are not necessary to the stated purpose and create a plausible cross-session prompt-injection path.\n[T05] unexpected: The dashboard's memory search, recent, stats, and delete endpoints trust caller-supplied wallet identifiers rather than authenticated ownership, so cross-wallet access is a real scoping concern if the service is reachable.\n[T09] unexpected: Several implementation defects are supported by artifact evidence, including default remote embeddings conflicting with privacy claims, fake transaction hashes granting Pro licenses, and quota checks treating a result object as a boolean.\n[E1] expected: The localhost fetch and curl examples are expected dashboard API examples, not evidence of covert exfiltration by themselves; the meaningful external-transmission concern is the OpenAI embedding path.\n[SSRF2] expected: The flagged localhost requests are documentation examples for calling the local dashboard API and do not independently show SSRF behavior.\n[E4] expected: The cited session-end code logs a local session summary and license/quota status; I did not find evidence there of external conversation-context transmission.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789063118126}}}}}